<title>CROATIA: TABLE - Croatian Privredna Banka's 1996 loss deepens.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Croatian Privredna Banka's 1996 loss deepens.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for calendar 1996.</p>
<p>Millions of kuna unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>					1996		  1995</p>
<p>    Net result		  (1,117)     vs	(208)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result	    (1,099)     vs	(207)</p>
<p>    Net operating result    (1,022)     vs	(184)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	    (77)     vs	 (23)</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  273	vs	 252</p>
<p>    Total income		   691	vs	 508</p>
<p>    Loan losses		   (399)     vs	(202)</p>
<p>    Writedown on investments  (767)     vs	 (25)</p>
<p>    Other operating loss	(547)     vs	(465)</p>
<p>    Risk asset ratio (pct)    14.8	vs	14.3</p>
<p>    Total assets (bln HRK)    14.86     vs	18.64</p>
<p>NOTE -- Results are for Privredna Banka Zagreb and its subsidiaries  Centar Banka, Riadria Banka and Laguna Banka.</p>
<p>The balance sheet reduction reflects a writeoff for uncollected debts  the government took over as part of Privredna's rehabilitation programme.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb newsroom, +385 1 455 7075</p>
</text>
